From: ashi009 <ashi009@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] config: protect Mihomo listeners from tailnet access

The tailnet zone accepts router-local input to preserve management access.
Restricting forwarding to LAN does not block a connection to Mihomo's
explicit proxy: the proxy opens its own outbound connection.

With protect-listeners enabled, deny tailnet access to Mihomo's proxy, DNS
and controller listeners. Derive ports from the parsed configuration so
UCI does not duplicate them. The option defaults to false; our Jsonnet
explicitly enables it.
---
diff --git a/config/config.go b/config/config.go
--- a/config/config.go
+++ b/config/config.go
@@ -643,7 +643,17 @@
 
 func ParseRawConfig(rawCfg *RawConfig) (*Config, error) {
 	config := &Config{}
-	tc, err := tailnet.Normalize(rawCfg.Tailnet)
+	dnsListener := ""
+	if rawCfg.DNS.Enable {
+		dnsListener = rawCfg.DNS.Listen
+	}
+	protectedTailnet, err := tailnet.ProtectListeners(rawCfg.Tailnet,
+		[]int{rawCfg.Port, rawCfg.SocksPort, rawCfg.MixedPort, rawCfg.RedirPort, rawCfg.TProxyPort}, rawCfg.Listeners,
+		rawCfg.ExternalController, rawCfg.ExternalControllerTLS, dnsListener)
+	if err != nil {
+		return nil, err
+	}
+	tc, err := tailnet.Normalize(protectedTailnet)
 	if err != nil {
 		return nil, err
 	}
